            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0546" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221 Dahl, Harold/24: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seville</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-04T12:00:00+01:00">August 4,
                        1937—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received August 4—10:17 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My August 3 [<hi rendition="#italic">2</hi>], noon.<anchor n="88"
                        xml:id="d506-f1"/> General Queipo de Llano stated this morning he would
                    communicate to General Franco the views of the Department concerning Harold Dahl
                    which I conveyed to him orally in accordance with the Department’s July 30, 5
                    p.m. He hinted that Dahl may be exchanged.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
